        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Infectious Music, Atlantic Records, Canvasback Music\n- People: alt-J, Ash, Symposium, My Vitriol, Seafood, The Paradise Motel, The Subways\n- Places: Welwyn Garden City, Hertfordshire, UK, U.S.\n- Products: Young for Eternity, Relaxer\n- Topics: record labels, rock bands, album releases\n\nFacts:\n- Infectious Music is a record label whose bands have included alt-J, Ash, Symposium, My Vitriol, Seafood, The Paradise Motel, and The Subways.\n- The Subways are an English rock band from Welwyn Garden City, Hertfordshire.\n- The Subways released their debut album Young for Eternity in the UK on 4 July 2005 and in the U.S. on 14 February 2006.\n- alt-J released their third studio album Relaxer on 2 June 2017 through Infectious Music and the Canvasback Music division of Atlantic Records.",
